		{
			"id": "114552172689525345",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://front-end.social/@eeeps/114552172668834669",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eric Portis",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@eeeps",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/304/428/669/626/974/original/f87ff3e52bb789da.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2025-05-22T15:23:59.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I'll leave the JS to someone else and just take the hero image; sizes=100vw is bad esp. on desktop; the img never gets above 690px wide, but is often serving the largest 3840w image (5.56x). Good news though: that image is actually only 1000 pixels wide. In fact, 5/8 of the urls in the srcset are only 1000 pixels wide. This is sloppy and has bad caching impacts, but arguably two wrongs make a right; that's better than serving a 5.5x image! (con't)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114552195839802463",
			"parentId": "114552172689525345",
			"url": "https://front-end.social/@eeeps/114552195822132043",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eric Portis",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@eeeps",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/304/428/669/626/974/original/f87ff3e52bb789da.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2025-05-22T15:29:52.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Similarly, while the URL says \"fm=webp\", I actually get a JPG. Maybe their image backend is smarter than their HTML author, and JPEG is actually a better choice for this image, but I doubt it. It's extremely high quality, especially for a black and white image: almost 3 bits/pixel. Here's a 1 bit-per-pixel AVIF which looks really good to my eye: <a href=\"https://o.img.rodeo/image/fetch/q_auto:best,f_avif/https://cdn.openai.com/sam-and-jony/portrait.jpg?w=3840&amp;q=90&amp;fm=webp\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">o.img.rodeo/image/fetch/q_auto</span><span class=\"invisible\">:best,f_avif/https://cdn.openai.com/sam-and-jony/portrait.jpg?w=3840&amp;q=90&amp;fm=webp</span></a> (con't)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
