			},
			"date": "2025-05-22T15:34:46.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Lastly, loading=lazy on the LCP-responsible img is a no good, very bad, shot-in-the-foot. But they're also fading the image in late which makes for a more cinematic-reveal-type-feel, which gives it a reason to come in late? idk. At least there's no layout shift.</p>",
