			"date": "2025-05-23T22:27:55.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@yvg\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>yvg</span></a></span> Jony says no to 1,000 things so he can say yes to 11MB of JavaScript</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114559573804058145",
			"parentId": "114559446065466986",
			"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff/114559573444576964",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alex Russell",
				"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/557/125/861/804/original/f19233215012175c.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-05-23T22:46:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Oh. My. God.</p><p>If the JS doesn't load, you can't see the ~2.8KB (1.4KB gzipped) of text *at all*.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114559573437803508",
			"parentId": "114559573804058145",
			"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff/114559573453112478",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alex Russell",
				"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/557/125/861/804/original/f19233215012175c.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-05-23T22:46:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p>The animations reliably jank on scroll...which takes doing when your're actually using CSS transitions (which they are!). How do you pull it off? Animate every section independently with what looks like custom intersection observer nonsense. It's intensely lame. You can scroll halfway down the page, hit \"reload\", and have most text fail to display because it doesn't animate in.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114559598111493789",
			"parentId": "114559469640105248",
			"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff/114559597988375506",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alex Russell",
				"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/557/125/861/804/original/f19233215012175c.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-05-23T22:52:20.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> \"Dear AI, how can I display 3K of text, one image, and a below-the-fold video in the slowest, least reliable way that maximally pads my resume?\"</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114559615114114896",
